# Description

Fixes https://github.com/agglayer/agglayer/issues/754

Aligns the commitment on the imported bridge exits which is involved in the signature and in the aggchain proof public values.

The following emphasize the difference between `V2` and `V3` for both commitments:
- imported bridge exit commitment
- certificate signature commitment (which involves the imported bridge exit commitment)

### Imported bridge exit commitment version

The `V3` of this commitment is introduced in the `interop` repo in https://github.com/agglayer/interop/pull/12

```rust
/// The values which compose the commitment on the imported bridge exits.
pub struct ImportedBridgeExitCommitmentValues {
    pub claims: Vec<GlobalIndexWithLeafHash>,
}

impl ImportedBridgeExitCommitmentValues {
    /// Returns the expected signed commitment for the provided version.
    pub fn commitment(&self, version: Version) -> Digest {
        match version {
            V2 => {
                // Commits solely to the global index of each imported bridge exit. Designed
                // prior to having any notion of aggchain proof.
                keccak256_combine(
                    self.claims
                        .iter()
                        .map(|ibe| keccak256(ibe.global_index.as_le_slice())),
                )
            }
            V3 => {
                // Adds the bridge exit hashes in the commitment to ensure that the aggchain
                // proof and PP talk about the exact same set of imported bridge exits.
                keccak256_combine(self.claims.iter().map(|ibe| {
                    [
                        ibe.global_index.as_le_slice(),
                        ibe.bridge_exit_hash.as_slice(),
                    ]
                    .concat()
                }))
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This commitment is involved in the certificate signature and also in the aggchain proof.

### Certificate signature version

```rust
/// The values which compose the signature.
pub struct SignatureCommitmentValues {
    pub new_local_exit_root: Digest,
    pub commit_imported_bridge_exits: ImportedBridgeExitCommitmentValues,
    pub height: u64,
}

impl SignatureCommitmentValues {
    /// Returns the expected signed commitment for the provided version.
    pub fn commitment(&self, version: Version) -> Digest {
        let imported_bridge_exit_commitment = self.commit_imported_bridge_exits.commitment(version);
        match version {
            V2 => keccak256_combine([
                self.new_local_exit_root.as_slice(),
                imported_bridge_exit_commitment.as_slice(),
            ]),
            V3 => keccak256_combine([
                self.new_local_exit_root.as_slice(),
                imported_bridge_exit_commitment.as_slice(),
                self.height.to_le_bytes().as_slice(),
            ]),
        }
    }
}
```

